From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ana Sollano Kim <ansollan@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:04:33 -0700
Subject: [EyeDropper] Respect captured frame row stride

The screen-capture callback sizes its bitmap using the frame dimensions
but copies height times the source stride. Padded source rows therefore
corrupt copied pixels and exceed the destination allocation.

Use Skia's stride-aware pixel copy and cover padded and tightly packed
frames with unit tests.

Bug: 571856431
Change-Id: I1252c131393c2f520208e965790c94458da13321
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8562038
Commit-Queue: Ana Sollano Kim <ansollan@microsoft.com>
Reviewed-by: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Dan Clark <daniec@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719954}

